<article class="env-notation" id="06WP">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06WP">Notation <span data-tag="06WP">9.6.6.27</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category equipped with diagrams $F: J \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $G: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Constructions <a data-tag="04J1" href="/tag/04J1">4.6.6.4</a> and <a data-tag="03JY" href="/tag/03JY">8.1.2.7</a> then supply comparison maps </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \{  F \}  \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(J, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{Fun}(J \star K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \leftarrow \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} ) \quad \quad \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} }( J^{\operatorname{op}}, \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(J^{\operatorname{op}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> which are equivalences of $\infty $-categories (Theorem <a data-tag="04J2" href="/tag/04J2">4.6.6.5</a> and Corollary <a data-tag="06TQ" href="/tag/06TQ">8.1.2.21</a>). Applying the construction $\operatorname{Fun}(K, \bullet )$ on the right hand side and passing to fibers over $G \in \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, we obtain a diagram of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \{  F \}  \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(J, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{Fun}(J \star K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \{ G\}  \leftarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( J^{\operatorname{op}} \times K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \]
</div>
<p> where both maps are homotopy equivalences (Corollary <a data-tag="01HK" href="/tag/01HK">4.5.3.31</a> and Remark <a data-tag="01HA" href="/tag/01HA">4.5.1.16</a>). Note that this diagram depends functorially on $J$ and $K$ (as objects of the category $(\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }})_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$). </p>
</article>
